WEBVTT

00:01.169 --> 00:04.643
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.710 --> 00:08.050
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.183 --> 00:11.757
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.823 --> 00:14.763
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.829 --> 00:18.203
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.269 --> 00:21.375
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.475 --> 00:23.113
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.179 --> 00:24.382
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.482 --> 00:30.327
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.471 --> 00:38.209
Good evening. Coming up,
a major Hollywood movie

00:38.309 --> 00:39.913
is set to film in Quahog.

00:39.980 --> 00:41.483
But first,
whoever recorded me

00:41.551 --> 00:43.587
cursing at
that freeway off-ramp veteran,

00:43.621 --> 00:45.826
please don't post that,
all right, seriously.

00:45.892 --> 00:47.495
We all have bad days.

00:47.529 --> 00:49.866
Our top story:
the latest Brad Pitt film

00:49.966 --> 00:51.504
will be shot
right here in Quahog.

00:51.571 --> 00:53.707
Pitt will play
former New Jersey governor

00:53.808 --> 00:54.543
Chris Christie.

00:54.643 --> 00:57.147
Brad Pitt is playing
Chris Christie?!

00:57.247 --> 00:59.252
It should be a fat guy
playing that role!

00:59.318 --> 01:02.458
Chris Christie didn't eat
10,000 Jersey Mike's subs

01:02.526 --> 01:04.763
just to be played
by a Hollywood pretty boy.

01:04.830 --> 01:07.903
That's offensive, and I,
for one, will not stand for it.

01:07.969 --> 01:10.842
Although that's mostly
due to cardiovascular disease.

01:10.909 --> 01:12.177
I got to sit down.

01:12.244 --> 01:14.248
Peter, you know, you've
actually got a valid point.

01:14.315 --> 01:16.285
Oh, boy. Here comes the soapbox.

01:16.419 --> 01:18.791
It's shameful Hollywood would
pass over the many talented

01:18.891 --> 01:21.864
plus-sized actors who are
much more deserving of the role.

01:21.931 --> 01:23.433
-Name two.
-Jonah Hill?

01:23.499 --> 01:25.137
-He's thin now.
-Uh, Fat Albert?

01:25.270 --> 01:26.540
-Not real.
-James Corden?

01:26.573 --> 01:28.310
He's been canceled
for sending eggs back.

01:28.410 --> 01:30.949
Well, it's just another example
of Hollywood's history

01:31.015 --> 01:32.553
of exclusionary casting,

01:32.619 --> 01:35.290
-whitewashing and thin-washing.
-Exactly.

01:35.356 --> 01:38.063
Like Mike Myers playing
an Indian man in The Love Guru.

01:38.163 --> 01:40.300
-[giggles]
-Or Marlon and Shawn Wayans

01:40.333 --> 01:42.371
-playing White Chicks.
-[giggles]

01:42.437 --> 01:44.509
Or Mickey Rooney playing
an offensive stereotype

01:44.576 --> 01:46.547
of an Asian man
in Breakfast at Tiffany's.

01:46.647 --> 01:48.818
I don't know that movie,
but I like breakfast.

01:48.918 --> 01:50.387
Oh, come on, you two.

01:50.454 --> 01:52.558
You're really offended that
one of the biggest movie stars

01:52.625 --> 01:56.165
on the planet is coming to
our crap town to shoot a movie?

01:56.232 --> 01:58.002
I mean, Brad Pitt could put it
anywhere,

01:58.069 --> 01:59.739
-with any of us.
-Facts.

01:59.773 --> 02:02.980
I mean, when was the last time
a celebrity visited Quahog?

02:03.046 --> 02:04.916
-Uh, Jared Fogle.
-Who?

02:04.983 --> 02:06.185
The Subway Guy. Remember?

02:06.285 --> 02:07.589
He was here
for a public appearance.

02:07.622 --> 02:09.058
Took a shine to Chris
for some reason.

02:09.125 --> 02:10.327
Took him camping.

02:10.393 --> 02:12.231
Had these weird candies
he'd only let Chris eat.

02:12.298 --> 02:14.536
How come I don't remember
any of this?

02:14.602 --> 02:16.339
Ah, too many video games,
buddy.

02:16.405 --> 02:17.909
They're rotting your brains.

02:17.976 --> 02:20.047
Get your hands off me, Jared!

02:20.114 --> 02:22.250
You're really gonna complain
about Brad Pitt?

02:22.317 --> 02:24.189
Who cares what role
he's playing?!

02:24.255 --> 02:25.758
Well, that's easy
for you to say, Lois.

02:25.825 --> 02:28.463
Women have no idea
what it's like for us men,

02:28.531 --> 02:30.802
being held up to
impossible standards of beauty

02:30.869 --> 02:31.737
in the media.

02:31.804 --> 02:33.975
Ooh, Jennifer Lawrence has
a new movie.

02:34.042 --> 02:35.512
Eh! Too old. Next.

02:35.579 --> 02:37.181
Peter, I think
you're right to protest.

02:37.248 --> 02:38.817
-I'll even join you.
-Thanks, Brian.

02:38.884 --> 02:41.656
Sometimes you just got
to stand up for what's right.

02:41.723 --> 02:43.728
That's why I stood up
to Kanye West.

02:43.794 --> 02:46.600
Dinosaurs were created
by the Illuminati.

02:46.667 --> 02:49.371
The government hides secrets
in SpaghettiOs.

02:49.438 --> 02:50.975
And Hitler would've
won Wimbledon

02:51.075 --> 02:52.746
if he played tennis, bro.

02:52.813 --> 02:54.582
Sir, sir, sir.

02:54.649 --> 02:57.588
We do not wear shoes
in this house.

02:58.690 --> 03:02.264
Thank you. Now please
continue about Wimbledon.

03:04.368 --> 03:06.273
[chanting]
Overweight is overdue!

03:06.339 --> 03:07.441
Overweight is overdue!

03:07.509 --> 03:09.445
Wow, I'm impressed, Peter.

03:09.512 --> 03:11.115
Yeah, it's going great.

03:11.182 --> 03:12.919
News trucks even showed up
to cover it.

03:12.986 --> 03:15.558
I-I think... I think those
are just food trucks.

03:15.658 --> 03:18.263
Come on, you know you want some.

03:18.329 --> 03:19.566
Hi, fellas.

03:19.633 --> 03:21.737
Oh, hey. Thanks for coming out
to support us.

03:21.837 --> 03:24.308
"Dangerous Curves Ahead."

03:25.477 --> 03:28.083
-Oh...
-[laughs] Right?

03:28.150 --> 03:30.287
[laughs]
Oh, that is good.

03:30.354 --> 03:32.124
[laughing]
You get it.

03:32.257 --> 03:34.896
[laughs]
That... that is clever.

03:34.996 --> 03:35.999
Am I right?

03:36.099 --> 03:37.268
[laughter]

03:37.334 --> 03:39.607
That, that's good.
That's good.

03:39.673 --> 03:41.843
-Isn't it, though? [laughs]
-Yeah, yeah.

03:41.910 --> 03:44.816
[whispers] Brian, can you
explain that shirt to me later?

03:48.323 --> 03:50.360
Protesters were on hand today
at the set of

03:50.427 --> 03:53.233
the new Chris Christie biopic
being filmed in Quahog.

03:53.299 --> 03:56.305
They were protesting the casting
of Hollywood superstar Brad Pitt

03:56.405 --> 03:59.244
in the lead role
and not a person of heft.

03:59.311 --> 04:01.415
Well, Peter, I'm just glad
you're on the news

04:01.516 --> 04:04.789
for something other than sitting
on a hamster at a school event.

04:04.889 --> 04:07.596
[clamoring]

04:07.696 --> 04:09.331
Hey, they said they weren't
gonna put that!

04:09.398 --> 04:10.668
[doorbell rings]

04:11.335 --> 04:13.173
Mr. Griffin, hi.

04:13.273 --> 04:14.910
I'm Josh Universal
from the movie.

04:15.010 --> 04:17.549
I'm taking a break
from my horrific cocaine habit

04:17.615 --> 04:19.586
to ask you
to sit down with our producers

04:19.652 --> 04:22.725
for a "listening session"
to hear your concerns.

04:22.792 --> 04:25.598
And, on an unrelated note,
can I use your bathroom,

04:25.699 --> 04:27.468
and does anyone have
a rolled-up bill?

04:27.569 --> 04:30.039
Oh, of course. I got
a special five just for that.

04:30.841 --> 04:34.516
[sniffs] All right, let's get
zapped and go see a play!

04:34.616 --> 04:36.653
♪ ♪

04:39.091 --> 04:41.295
Hmm. That's odd.

04:46.540 --> 04:48.778
Mr. Griffin, thank you
for meeting with us.

04:48.844 --> 04:49.946
Have a seat.

04:50.013 --> 04:51.382
Not on my lap!

04:51.482 --> 04:53.085
Sorry. [chuckles]
I'm a little nervous.

04:53.186 --> 04:55.824
Peter Griffin,
please meet Brad Pitt.

04:56.325 --> 04:58.564
♪ ♪

04:59.566 --> 05:01.637
[gasps]
George Clooney's boyfriend?

05:01.704 --> 05:04.375
No, no. A few years ago,
he was cast in a marriage.

05:04.442 --> 05:06.246
Mr. Griffin,
we've asked you here

05:06.312 --> 05:07.816
because we understand
you have an issue

05:07.916 --> 05:09.853
with Brad playing the lead role
in our movie.

05:09.920 --> 05:13.594
We want to make sure we hear
and ignore all your concerns.

05:13.694 --> 05:16.232
Look, I know Brad Pitt is
a big star and all,

05:16.299 --> 05:18.369
but he's playing Chris Christie,
who's a fat guy.

05:18.469 --> 05:21.142
It seems unfair that
the role didn't go to a fat guy.

05:21.209 --> 05:22.377
It only makes sense.

05:22.477 --> 05:24.549
Don't you think
we should cast the best actor,

05:24.616 --> 05:25.952
letting them interpret the role,

05:26.052 --> 05:27.922
rather than depending
on physical traits?

05:28.022 --> 05:30.394
Not if you're taking the role
away from a fat guy.

05:30.460 --> 05:33.066
But, Mr. Griffin, Brad Pitt is
a highly skilled actor

05:33.166 --> 05:36.406
who's won an Oscar and lots
of garbage Golden Globes.

05:36.507 --> 05:37.876
You're not hearing my concerns.

05:37.943 --> 05:39.913
You don't know
the challenges fat guys face.

05:40.046 --> 05:42.083
What it's like
to have to rock multiple times

05:42.183 --> 05:44.488
to get off the couch,
or how it feels to have to poke

05:44.556 --> 05:46.425
a new hole in your belt
with a nail,

05:46.492 --> 05:48.429
only to realize
the end no longer

05:48.462 --> 05:49.733
tucks into the little loop,

05:49.833 --> 05:51.302
or the shame
of getting thrown out

05:51.369 --> 05:52.639
of a strip club for touching.

05:52.706 --> 05:54.743
That last thing doesn't seem
like a weight issue.

05:54.810 --> 05:56.513
You sound just like the judge!

05:56.614 --> 05:59.418
Look, the casting of this movie
is offensive to fat people,

05:59.520 --> 06:02.023
and I won't rest
until it gets shut down.

06:03.259 --> 06:04.663
Mr. Griffin, look,

06:04.730 --> 06:08.269
what if we made you our
"official fat guy consultant"?

06:08.369 --> 06:09.973
Do you think I'm an idiot?

06:10.073 --> 06:11.677
Yes! What if I told you

06:11.710 --> 06:14.549
we'll give you a P.A. who will
get you anything you want?

06:14.616 --> 06:16.419
Deal. 20 Happy Meals, please.

06:16.520 --> 06:18.591
He's actually Judd Apatow's
nephew Zack.

06:18.658 --> 06:20.127
You can't tell him what to do.

06:20.260 --> 06:21.529
In fact, you work for him.

06:21.563 --> 06:22.899
I want you to get me this thing,

06:22.999 --> 06:25.437
and I can't remember
what it is or where I saw it.

06:25.505 --> 06:28.510
Wow, I'm gonna learn so much
from his last name.

06:34.288 --> 06:36.492
[fighting and gunfire on TV]

06:37.762 --> 06:40.066
The new season of White Lotus
is weird.

06:40.133 --> 06:42.672
Griffins, you are looking at
the Chris Christie movie's

06:42.738 --> 06:44.843
official fat guy consultant.

06:44.910 --> 06:47.682
Boy, that's a garbage title
if I ever heard one.

06:47.749 --> 06:49.719
What? Wait a minute,
so instead of demanding

06:49.819 --> 06:51.890
they cast a plus-sized actor,
you caved

06:51.957 --> 06:53.727
when they offered you
a meaningless title?

06:53.794 --> 06:56.231
-What about
everything you fought for?
-Don't you see, Brian?

06:56.298 --> 06:59.338
Now I can work the system
from the inside with dignity.

06:59.404 --> 07:02.044
-[phone rings]
-Yes, Mr. Apatow's nephew?

07:02.846 --> 07:05.216
[deflated]
Yes, Mr. Apatow's nephew.

07:06.252 --> 07:08.724
[crying]
Yes, Mr. Apatow's nephew.

07:08.791 --> 07:10.995
What does a fat guy consultant
even do?

07:11.062 --> 07:13.734
I'm the personal
weight-gain coach for Brad Pitt.

07:13.834 --> 07:15.370
Wou-Would we get to meet him?

07:15.437 --> 07:17.642
Sure. My job is
to teach him how to think,

07:17.742 --> 07:19.513
eat and live like a fat guy.

07:19.580 --> 07:21.216
So, just like that,
you're giving up?

07:21.282 --> 07:22.618
Brian, I'm a fat guy.

07:22.685 --> 07:23.988
I got all fired up
about something,

07:24.088 --> 07:26.960
and now I'm tired
and I'd like some custard.

07:30.534 --> 07:33.540
Guys, I'd like you to meet
my new friend Brad Pitt.

07:33.640 --> 07:36.011
-Oh, my God!
-Whoa, nice to meet you.

07:36.111 --> 07:38.651
-Who's this now?
-He's a very famous actor.

07:38.684 --> 07:40.521
He's like
the white Morris Chestnut.

07:40.621 --> 07:42.424
-Oh, damn!
-Wow!

07:42.525 --> 07:44.730
I can't believe I'm sitting here
with Brad Pitt.

07:44.796 --> 07:46.065
I've got so many questions.

07:46.131 --> 07:48.570
Like, what are the other rules
of Fight Club?

07:48.637 --> 07:50.107
Well, the first rule is--

07:50.207 --> 07:51.610
No, I'm clear on the first rule.

07:51.710 --> 07:54.448
And I know the second rule is
just repeating the first.

07:54.516 --> 07:55.785
But there's got to be
loads more.

07:55.885 --> 07:59.257
Like, I got to think
"no sack attacks" is on there.

07:59.291 --> 08:00.527
Hey, Brad.
Any chance I could get

08:00.628 --> 08:02.397
Jennifer Aniston's number
from you?

08:02.497 --> 08:03.701
I know she's got to be
a nightmare,

08:03.801 --> 08:06.172
but she keeps it
so freakin' tight.

08:06.238 --> 08:07.240
Okay, enough small talk.

08:07.340 --> 08:08.677
Let's do
what I brought him here for:

08:08.744 --> 08:10.581
to break the Internet
with a group

08:10.681 --> 08:13.386
-head-smushed-together selfie.
-[phone beeps]

08:13.521 --> 08:14.822
[camera clicks]

08:14.889 --> 08:17.562
Kevin Spacey?
Get out of here.

08:17.662 --> 08:19.699
You're not allowed to be
in head-smushed-together photos

08:19.766 --> 08:20.768
after what you did.

08:20.835 --> 08:23.507
Not guilty
on all British counts.

08:23.573 --> 08:26.078
[chuckles] Oh, that rascal.

08:29.085 --> 08:30.955
[knocking]

08:31.055 --> 08:34.061
Hi, you must be Peter's wife.
I'm Brad.

08:34.161 --> 08:36.165
♪ ♪

08:37.400 --> 08:40.575
Oh, I know who you are.
I'm-- [screams]

08:40.675 --> 08:42.512
Hi, I'm-- [screams]

08:42.579 --> 08:43.981
Stewart. Charmed.

08:44.048 --> 08:45.717
I know you dump people
when they're 40,

08:45.784 --> 08:48.624
but that still gives us
39 good years.

08:48.724 --> 08:50.728
Pleased to meet you, Mr. Pitt.

08:50.828 --> 08:52.899
Um, when you did
that movie Snatch,

08:52.966 --> 08:55.036
did you know
that also means something else?

08:55.136 --> 08:56.707
Because it very much does.

08:56.807 --> 08:59.244
That's a sticky handshake
you got there, Chris.

08:59.311 --> 09:01.215
Peter, I was wondering
if I could spend some time

09:01.281 --> 09:03.821
with you and your family,
observing how you live

09:03.888 --> 09:06.292
and how you eat,
to prepare for the role.

09:06.359 --> 09:07.695
Sure, I'd be glad to help.

09:07.795 --> 09:09.933
Wow, I ain't had a celebrity
ask me for a favor

09:10.033 --> 09:12.705
since Jeremy Renner asked me
to shovel out his driveway.

09:12.805 --> 09:16.580
-[engine idling]
-Uh, Jeremy, in light of
recent events, uh...

09:16.647 --> 09:19.151
could ol' Pete borrow your skis?

09:21.957 --> 09:24.762
Okay, Brad, I'm gonna teach you
to be a fat guy.

09:24.863 --> 09:26.900
For starters,
this is where we eat.

09:26.966 --> 09:29.972
Um, excuse me, Mr. Pitt,
but would you mind

09:30.073 --> 09:31.910
if I FaceTime my friends
with you here?

09:31.977 --> 09:34.181
Oh, my God, they'll go crazy!

09:34.281 --> 09:35.851
Sure, Meg, it'd be my pleasure.

09:35.918 --> 09:38.757
-[squeals]
-[FaceTime app ringing]

09:48.042 --> 09:49.712
Oh, boy.

09:50.715 --> 09:53.085
Oh, this-this is sad.

09:54.522 --> 09:58.095
Oh, this-this is just... Oh...

09:58.195 --> 10:00.634
Why don't I just take this,
dear.

10:00.734 --> 10:02.337
-[ringing stops]
-[phone beeps]

10:06.813 --> 10:09.018
Okay, Brad, now,
another fat guy rule is that

10:09.118 --> 10:11.088
when you're out at restaurants,
always act like

10:11.155 --> 10:12.759
you're on the fence
about dessert.

10:12.826 --> 10:14.896
So, folks, we thinking dessert?

10:14.930 --> 10:16.800
Seriously? You must be joking.

10:16.900 --> 10:19.639
I cannot move.
No, sir. No way.

10:19.706 --> 10:21.510
Absolutely stuffed to the gills.

10:21.577 --> 10:22.912
Gonna have to take a rain check.

10:23.012 --> 10:25.116
Although... No, no,
I can't even suggest it.

10:25.217 --> 10:28.623
We are done. Done-a-roo.
Check, please.

10:28.690 --> 10:30.093
Although... just thinking,

10:30.160 --> 10:31.663
I don't know when
we'll be back here.

10:31.763 --> 10:33.667
I read about
the award-winning pastry chef--

10:33.734 --> 10:35.403
Wait, what am I saying? No! No.

10:35.504 --> 10:37.006
Stop me, please,
someone, please.

10:37.140 --> 10:38.443
Bring the check now.

10:38.544 --> 10:40.748
Okay, you know what, we'll get
one order and we'll all share.

10:40.848 --> 10:42.852
One dessert, one dish,
five spoons.

10:42.952 --> 10:44.155
Whoever wants can have some.

10:44.221 --> 10:46.325
One plate. One of everything.
My plate.

10:46.392 --> 10:48.395
One spoon. No share.

10:51.102 --> 10:53.039
Now, Brad, if you're gonna
play a fat guy on camera,

10:53.106 --> 10:55.911
you got to learn
how to do the rope swing.

10:58.116 --> 10:59.919
Okay, let me show you
how it's done.

11:00.721 --> 11:02.257
[groans]

11:05.263 --> 11:07.467
900,000 views.

11:07.535 --> 11:09.672
-I'm learning so much.
-That's great.

11:09.772 --> 11:11.676
Hey, can you click
on a porn site for me?

11:11.743 --> 11:13.279
Otherwise I got to
peck it with my nose

11:13.345 --> 11:15.316
like a tic-tac-toe chicken.

11:21.796 --> 11:23.634
Here you go.

11:23.701 --> 11:25.203
Thanks so much, Mrs. Griffin.

11:25.303 --> 11:26.806
I love a home-cooked meal.

11:26.873 --> 11:29.512
Well, we are
so happy to have you.

11:29.579 --> 11:30.981
-How's Shiloh?
-Who?

11:31.048 --> 11:32.518
-How's Maddox?
-Who?

11:32.585 --> 11:34.221
-How's Zahara?
-Who?

11:34.287 --> 11:35.624
-How's Pax?
-Who?

11:35.691 --> 11:36.960
-How's Vivienne?
-Who?

11:36.993 --> 11:38.228
-How's Knox?
-Who?

11:38.295 --> 11:40.133
Ignore her,
she can be so annoying.

11:40.200 --> 11:42.004
Sometimes I wish
I had a private plane

11:42.104 --> 11:44.140
just so I could choke her on it.

11:47.748 --> 11:49.084
Hey, can I get you anything?

11:49.184 --> 11:52.357
Another pork-n-Cheetos sandwich
or a buffalo latte?

11:52.423 --> 11:53.627
I'm good, Peter, thanks.

11:53.693 --> 11:55.196
[director]
Brad, you're up!

11:55.330 --> 11:56.498
[groans]

11:56.566 --> 11:58.870
[grunting]

11:58.970 --> 12:01.041
-Ah!
-[director] Brad? Are you okay?

12:01.108 --> 12:03.747
My back. I threw out my back.
I can't move.

12:03.814 --> 12:05.483
Hey, since you can't
really move right now,

12:05.551 --> 12:07.253
this is probably
a good time to ask,

12:07.320 --> 12:09.191
what's Juliette Lewis
really like?

12:09.291 --> 12:12.263
[straining]
Nice. Talented. Professional.

12:12.330 --> 12:15.136
-A little shrill.
-Yeah, a little shrill.
Yeah, that sounds right.

12:15.938 --> 12:18.643
[groaning, panting]

12:18.710 --> 12:20.915
I don't think I can walk.

12:20.948 --> 12:22.885
We can't push back our schedule
any more.

12:22.918 --> 12:24.855
If Brad's injured,
what are we gonna do?

12:24.889 --> 12:26.425
We'll need a new Chris Christie.

12:26.492 --> 12:29.999
But who could possibly play
that role on such short notice?

12:31.435 --> 12:32.771
I can play that role.

12:32.838 --> 12:34.843
Griffin,
you're not even an actor.

12:34.910 --> 12:37.615
No, but what I am is
a real fat guy.

12:37.682 --> 12:39.150
Brad Pitt was never
the right choice.

12:39.217 --> 12:42.324
This role calls for
real-life fat guy authenticity.

12:42.357 --> 12:44.227
I mean, would Transparent
have been as good

12:44.294 --> 12:45.965
if they just put a guy
in a dress?

12:46.065 --> 12:47.868
Would Neil Patrick Harris
have been as funny

12:47.969 --> 12:49.506
on How I Met Your Mother
if he wasn't

12:49.606 --> 12:51.342
a known heterosexual horndog?

12:51.442 --> 12:53.313
Would Tropic Thunder
have been as authentic

12:53.413 --> 12:56.953
if Robert Downey Jr. wasn't
a dignified Black man?

12:57.855 --> 12:59.559
We're in a jam.
What do you think?

12:59.692 --> 13:01.529
I don't think
we have any other choice.

13:01.663 --> 13:03.734
All right, Griffin,
you got the part.

13:03.834 --> 13:05.837
Awesome! I'm gonna
FaceTime my friends.

13:05.871 --> 13:07.575
They're gonna be
so excited for me.

13:07.641 --> 13:09.979
[FaceTime app ringing]

13:13.787 --> 13:15.489
Oh, boy.

13:16.693 --> 13:18.462
Oh, this-this is sad.

13:24.208 --> 13:26.479
[TV announcer]
We now return to
a steamy business drama

13:26.546 --> 13:28.550
where no one understands
what's happening.

13:28.616 --> 13:31.422
Are you saying we should forge
the EBITDA projections

13:31.489 --> 13:32.858
-for the quarterlies?
-No.

13:32.958 --> 13:34.529
I'm saying
we declare a revenue-miss

13:34.595 --> 13:36.098
while issuing additional shares

13:36.164 --> 13:38.570
based on reduced
capitalization estimates.

13:38.704 --> 13:40.674
Jim, you're in grave danger

13:40.741 --> 13:42.410
of violating
the Glass-Steagall Act.

13:42.477 --> 13:44.982
[Chris]
They haven't shown a bare ass
in three weeks!

13:45.082 --> 13:46.753
Show me your ass, Jim.

13:46.820 --> 13:47.989
[Chris]
And I'm back.

13:48.055 --> 13:50.861
Griffins,
you are looking at the new lead

13:50.961 --> 13:52.765
in the Chris Christie movie.

13:52.799 --> 13:55.403
You? Wh-What happened
to Brad Pitt?

13:55.469 --> 13:57.508
It's what I've been saying
all along, Lois.

13:57.608 --> 13:58.844
He can't do what I do.

13:58.911 --> 14:00.881
He doesn't bring
the fat guy authenticity.

14:00.981 --> 14:03.019
His sweat doesn't smell
like french fries.

14:03.119 --> 14:05.056
He doesn't bring
the sky-high blood pressure

14:05.156 --> 14:06.726
or the jolting sleep apnea.

14:06.826 --> 14:08.730
I have that gift.
That's why.

14:08.797 --> 14:10.734
Peter, this is ridiculous.

14:10.868 --> 14:12.437
You can't play Chris Christie.

14:12.505 --> 14:14.341
You're not even an actor.

14:14.374 --> 14:15.578
Oh, no?

14:15.644 --> 14:19.418
Yes, Lois! Yes! Yes! Oh!

14:19.485 --> 14:20.855
Sound familiar?

14:20.921 --> 14:22.925
-But how do you...?
-Squirt gun full of Ivory.

14:23.025 --> 14:26.499
Sorry, Lunchables, I'm afraid
I've lost my appetite.

14:26.633 --> 14:27.902
Peter, I'm proud of you.

14:27.935 --> 14:29.304
You're actually making
important strides

14:29.404 --> 14:31.876
on behalf of inclusivity
and cultural sensitivity.

14:31.943 --> 14:33.146
Yeah, I'm all for that stuff.

14:33.279 --> 14:34.715
As long as we don't
got to take down

14:34.782 --> 14:36.185
the Confederate statue
in the yard.

14:36.285 --> 14:38.021
That's for history and learning.

14:38.088 --> 14:39.626
Even if they did
come in second place

14:39.692 --> 14:41.194
out of two armies in a war.

14:41.295 --> 14:44.268
-So, how'd we do?
-Second place, baby.

14:44.368 --> 14:45.771
Hey, not bad.

14:45.871 --> 14:48.408
Silver medal. Whoo!

14:51.983 --> 14:54.221
Okay, Peter,
so, in this next scene,

14:54.321 --> 14:57.293
Christie would probably struggle
in the heat and sun

14:57.360 --> 14:59.131
on the George Washington Bridge.

14:59.197 --> 15:01.803
You presume to lecture me
what it's like?

15:01.870 --> 15:04.041
How dare you thinsplain to me?

15:04.108 --> 15:06.780
Talk to me
when your BMI is over 35.

15:06.846 --> 15:08.783
Wow, a real live movie set.

15:08.850 --> 15:10.854
So cool to be here
for the magic.

15:10.921 --> 15:12.658
Yeah, and look,
there's a child star

15:12.725 --> 15:14.060
who's getting an hour of school.

15:14.161 --> 15:16.799
Okay, Billy, now,
what color is this?

15:16.833 --> 15:18.537
-Blue?
-Close enough.

15:18.603 --> 15:19.572
Now get back out there

15:19.639 --> 15:22.512
and be the most distracting
part of any film.

15:22.578 --> 15:23.747
♪ ♪

15:23.813 --> 15:25.751
♪ Making a movie ♪

15:25.817 --> 15:29.057
♪ Not as glamorous as it seems ♪

15:29.124 --> 15:30.561
♪ Standing around ♪

15:30.628 --> 15:33.065
♪ For three hours
just to move a light ♪

15:33.131 --> 15:36.640
♪ Tripping over thick cables
everywhere ♪

15:36.706 --> 15:42.150
♪ Spending all day shooting
one ten-second scene, yeah ♪

15:42.216 --> 15:46.191
♪ Waving flies
off the craft service table ♪

15:47.795 --> 15:49.231
♪ Making a movie ♪

15:49.331 --> 15:52.572
♪ Way more tedious
than it seems ♪

15:52.672 --> 15:56.311
♪ The most important job
is the editor ♪

15:56.411 --> 16:00.320
♪ Staring at a frame
for 18 hours straight ♪

16:00.420 --> 16:03.694
♪ Most of them snap
and go crazy ♪

16:03.794 --> 16:08.804
♪ Even a dumb cartoon like this
takes 18 months ♪

16:08.871 --> 16:13.412
♪ What are we all doing? ♪

16:17.320 --> 16:19.190
[camera shutters clicking]

16:19.257 --> 16:21.729
Oh, Peter,
your big movie premiere.

16:21.863 --> 16:23.465
This is so exciting!

16:23.566 --> 16:26.405
Did Dr. Hartman bring a woman
in a coma as his date?

16:26.540 --> 16:29.512
Hey, guys, big night, huh?
See you in there.

16:29.578 --> 16:31.583
-[crowd clamoring]
-[camera shutters clicking]

16:31.649 --> 16:34.989
Oh, God, here come those
mindless entertainment reporters

16:35.056 --> 16:36.892
who only want to know,
"Who are you wearing?"

16:36.993 --> 16:38.697
-Stewie!
-Stewie.
-Over here, Stewie.

16:38.764 --> 16:41.101
How do you respond to those
who accuse your show

16:41.168 --> 16:43.239
of trafficking in
decades of misogyny,

16:43.306 --> 16:46.011
homophobia and racially
insensitive stereotyping?

16:46.145 --> 16:48.650
Uh... Thom Browne, thank you.

16:48.717 --> 16:50.052
Go, Brian. Go, go, go, go, go.

16:50.152 --> 16:52.791
And here's the star of the film,
Peter Griffin.

16:52.891 --> 16:54.293
What are you wearing tonight,
Peter?

16:54.327 --> 16:57.167
Well, Tom, the shirt is actually
two shirts sewn together.

16:57.233 --> 16:59.605
The jacket is stolen
from a steak house maître d',

16:59.672 --> 17:01.207
and the pants are a towel.

17:01.241 --> 17:03.813
You know, I hear you were
quite the prankster on set.

17:03.880 --> 17:04.983
Well, it wasn't so much pranks

17:05.083 --> 17:06.285
as yelling
and shouting at women.

17:06.352 --> 17:07.754
Yeah, a lot of 'em aren't here
tonight.

17:07.821 --> 17:10.326
They're doing some town hall
meeting with Gloria Allred.

17:10.392 --> 17:12.229
Ah, we'll see what happens.

17:17.340 --> 17:18.577
The after-party's at a Panera

17:18.644 --> 17:21.281
that's still open
to normal customers.

17:21.381 --> 17:23.620
[cheering]

17:23.687 --> 17:25.055
Thank you all for coming.

17:25.189 --> 17:26.959
-[Quagmire] Giggity.
-It was a lot of hard work.

17:27.026 --> 17:30.233
-[Quagmire] Giggity.
-And thanks to the unnecessarily
long writers' strike,

17:30.299 --> 17:33.439
we were unable to write
a third joke for this speech.

17:33.540 --> 17:35.076
[cheering]

17:35.143 --> 17:36.979
-Hey!
-Ow!

17:37.046 --> 17:38.249
That's your father's movie
up there.

17:38.315 --> 17:39.953
Pay attention, you dope.

17:40.019 --> 17:42.256
♪ ♪

17:43.894 --> 17:46.398
[clamoring on screen]

17:47.500 --> 17:48.503
Repeat after me.

17:48.637 --> 17:51.308
-I's am governor.
-I's am governor.

17:51.375 --> 17:53.980
-Youse are not.
-Youse are not.

17:54.014 --> 17:56.719
Big Pussy didn't deserve
to die like that

17:56.786 --> 17:58.055
in The Sopranos.

17:58.122 --> 17:59.424
But he was a freakin' rat!

17:59.525 --> 18:02.096
Congratulations, you are
the governor of New Jersey.

18:02.163 --> 18:04.300
Now let's all root
for the Jets and the Mets

18:04.400 --> 18:06.104
like the idiots we are.

18:06.204 --> 18:08.308
[cheering]

18:08.408 --> 18:10.479
♪ ♪

18:11.616 --> 18:14.120
[thunder crashing]

18:15.390 --> 18:18.395
Lord, please protect us
from this coming hurricane.

18:18.496 --> 18:21.302
It's bad enough you gave me
the same first and last name.

18:21.402 --> 18:23.740
Please don't let me be killed
by a Sandy.

18:23.806 --> 18:27.715
The fellas at the Y would never
let me hear the end of it. Amen.

18:27.848 --> 18:29.886
♪ ♪

18:29.953 --> 18:31.857
[crying]

18:31.923 --> 18:34.394
Oh, Chris, you're dying.

18:34.494 --> 18:36.899
Don't remember me like this.

18:36.999 --> 18:39.104
Remember me stuffed
like a sausage

18:39.171 --> 18:41.976
into that NYPD softball uniform.

18:42.042 --> 18:44.782
♪ But I would walk 500 miles ♪

18:44.849 --> 18:48.623
-[scattered clapping]
-♪ And I would walk 500. ♪

18:49.792 --> 18:51.562
[feigning enthusiasm]
Hey, that was terrific.

18:51.629 --> 18:54.167
[forced]
Oh, what an achievement.

18:54.233 --> 18:55.704
[chuckles awkwardly]
You really did it, buddy.

18:55.770 --> 18:57.608
What are you guys
talking about? I stunk.

18:57.708 --> 18:58.743
I can't act at all.

18:58.843 --> 19:00.145
No...

19:00.212 --> 19:03.285
You were, uh,
very believably fat.

19:03.352 --> 19:04.922
Didn't you notice half the time

19:04.989 --> 19:06.425
I was staring
right into the camera?

19:06.491 --> 19:09.030
They had to use peanut butter
to get me on my mark.

19:09.097 --> 19:10.399
Yeah, but you've done
a great thing

19:10.466 --> 19:12.403
for authenticity
and inclusivity.

19:12.470 --> 19:13.740
I don't even know
what those words mean,

19:13.840 --> 19:16.077
I just like to see your tail wag
when you say 'em.

19:16.177 --> 19:18.717
Peter, you're giving
the marginalized a voice.

19:18.817 --> 19:20.086
How are they marginalized?

19:20.186 --> 19:22.323
The whole country's full
of dumb, fat [bleep].

19:22.457 --> 19:25.664
Now more than ever, we need
authenticity and inclusivity.

19:25.731 --> 19:28.069
No, Brian.
What we need is good actors.

19:28.169 --> 19:29.839
I don't care if they're Black,
white, tall,

19:29.906 --> 19:31.208
short, thin, fat.

19:31.275 --> 19:32.712
Gay, straight--
you forgot those ones.

19:32.812 --> 19:35.049
Look, I-I admit
I thought acting was easy.

19:35.149 --> 19:37.220
And maybe I was blinded
by all the praise I got

19:37.320 --> 19:38.523
from Harvey Weinstein.

19:38.590 --> 19:41.729
Peter, Harvey Weinstein hasn't
had clout for like six years.

19:41.863 --> 19:44.434
Oh, boy. Then I may have done
some things I'll regret.

19:45.035 --> 19:47.407
I don't know, I guess,
as a fat guy, I-I got offended

19:47.473 --> 19:49.579
that Chris Christie wasn't
played by a fat guy.

19:49.679 --> 19:52.116
But turns out it just needed
to be a good actor.

19:52.183 --> 19:54.221
Maybe we should all
spend less time judging

19:54.287 --> 19:55.490
and more time enjoying

19:55.591 --> 19:57.460
what different actors
bring to different roles.

19:57.561 --> 19:59.898
That's the magic
of movies and TV.

19:59.998 --> 20:01.368
[Chris]
And stepson porn.

20:01.502 --> 20:03.740
Chris, you don't have
to join every conversation.

20:03.840 --> 20:06.111
[murmuring]

20:06.211 --> 20:07.480
Okay, look, look, I understand

20:07.548 --> 20:09.552
not everyone will agree
on this issue,

20:09.619 --> 20:11.622
but let's discuss it
in a civilized manner

20:11.689 --> 20:14.094
by making death threats
from our individual homes

20:14.194 --> 20:15.964
to one another on the Internet.

20:16.031 --> 20:17.834
[phone chimes]

20:20.440 --> 20:21.809
Right back at you, buddy.

20:27.587 --> 20:30.527
Well, I'm sorry your movie
didn't go over well, Peter.

20:30.627 --> 20:32.129
Yeah, the money was good,
but I got tired of

20:32.196 --> 20:33.365
all the one-night stands.

20:33.432 --> 20:34.367
-What?
-Huh?

20:34.434 --> 20:35.837
Sorry, my ears have been clogged

20:35.904 --> 20:37.941
since I made out with that guy
from the film crew.

20:38.008 --> 20:39.111
-What?
-Huh?

20:39.177 --> 20:40.245
Well, I got to say, Bri,

20:40.312 --> 20:41.516
it might not have worked out
for Dad,

20:41.583 --> 20:43.887
but I sure got bit
by the acting bug.

20:43.954 --> 20:45.256
Really? You want to be an actor?

20:45.390 --> 20:47.828
Oh, yeah. I'd be great
in Streetcar.

20:47.895 --> 20:51.569
Stella! Stella!

20:51.635 --> 20:52.971
What?!

20:53.038 --> 20:55.342
Is Aidan home?